  "solution": {
    "text": "(1)  <math><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  has higher boiling point than  <math><mtext>As</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  and  <math><mtext>P</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  on account  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>  ‐bonding.  <math><mtext>Sb</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  has highest boiling point on account of highest molecular weight.<br/><br/>(2) As the size of element increases, the strength of M‐H bond decreases and thus stability decreases.<br/><br/>(3) Basicity decreases down the group. (Drago rule).<br/><br/>        (4) HEH angle  <math><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∘</mo></mrow></msup></math> )  <math><mo>:</mo><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>107.8</mn><mo>;</mo><mtext>P</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>93.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>As</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>91.8</mn><mo>;</mo><mtext>Sb</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>91.3</mn><mo>.</mo></math>"
